- Rules read the 3-dim RegimeLabel. unknown/warm-up dimensions make a gated rule fall
  through to restricted (conservative); "no-gate" families (sector_rotation,
  long_term_etf, cash_reserve) are always permitted; deferred families (event_driven,
  volatility) always restricted.
- Matrix: trend_following/momentum = bull & vol!=extreme; breakouts = bull & breadth in
  {expansion,neutral}; pullback = bull & breadth==neutral; mean_reversion = trend in
  {neutral,bear} & breadth in {neutral,contraction}. cash_reserve_boost = bear & extreme
  (an allocation signal for portfolio/allocation, not a position gate).
- Bug found+fixed: gate_positions must pass positions.index to attach_regimes (whose
  contract is Index|DataFrame); passing the Series mis-reindexed every bar to unknown and
  flattened everything. Regression covered by the gating tests.

