    correlations via update_metrics). Export from portfolio/__init__.py.
[x] Tests: tests/test_risk_budget.py (12) + tests/test_correlation.py (6).

Design notes:
- Heat = risk-at-stop (fraction of account equity lost if stopped), NOT dollar exposure.
  Position with no stop_price contributes 0 heat (must be caught by weight/DD checks).
- Per-strategy heat budget = (capital_alloc/account_equity) * max_portfolio_heat;
  suspend when |drawdown_cur| > max_drawdown OR strategy_heat > its budget.
- risk_contributions = each strategy's share of total portfolio heat (sums to 1; 0 when no
  heat). apply_/update_ledger_* write back onto ledgers via the §7 update_metrics hook.
- correlation: Pearson on the common calendar via DataFrame.corr(); average_correlation is
  a single diversification gauge; flag_high_correlation surfaces hidden concentration.

