Date: 2026-06-26
Goal: Implement the multi-model family abstraction (families/base.py + registry.py, §11).

Tasks:
[x] families/registry.py: (family,name) registry mirroring estimators/registry —
    register_model decorator, get_model, create_model, list_models(family|None),
    list_families, all_models.
[x] families/base.py: Model (ABC: signals(prices) -> positions; backtest() reuses
    signals.backtest, tags meta with family/model); EstimatorModel (concrete base composing
    a named estimator+deviation+window+signal = the existing pipeline; per-instance
    window/signal override); StrategyFamily (model_names/create/create_all over the
    registry). Re-exports register_model.
[x] families/mean_reversion/models.py: ZScoreReversionModel (sma/zscore/20) registered as
    mean_reversion/zscore_reversion — proves the pattern; other 4 MR models left TODO.
[x] families/__init__: export base+registry API; side-effect import of mean_reversion.models
    to populate the registry on package import.
[x] Tests: tests/test_families.py (8).

Design notes:
- A registered model inherits the whole validation/scoring/graduation stack for free:
  Model.backtest reuses signals.backtest, and the test asserts model.backtest(...).returns
  EQUALS run_backtest('sma','zscore',window=20) — i.e. zero new pipeline, just a named
  composition. EstimatorModel subclasses only declare estimator/deviation/window.
- Registry mirrors estimators/registry exactly (decorator sets cls.family/cls.name, dup
  key raises). Registration is a side-effect of importing each family's models module.
- Only mean_reversion has a concrete model so far; adding models to other families is now
  a one-class, one-decorator job (no infra changes).

